     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>In the code below, the plot changes depending on whether &quot;All Typists&quot; is selected or not. When it is selected, the app looks like this, a scatter plot with a trend line:</div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-K-k4GaTbcBU/VzUh45_4RMI/AAAAAAAAIn4/3yT5gQMi6mketK1Aad-_qiZoYvH7VU9sACLcB/s1600/Screen%2BShot%2B2016-05-12%2Bat%2B11.49.02%2BAM.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-K-k4GaTbcBU/VzUh45_4RMI/AAAAAAAAIn4/3yT5gQMi6mketK1Aad-_qiZoYvH7VU9sACLcB/s1600/Screen%252BShot%252B2016-05-12%252Bat%252B11.49.02%252BAM.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393551178000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10ZNomPuT-yPeh8RCoOhJt\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-K-k4GaTbcBU/VzUh45_4RMI/AAAAAAAAIn4/3yT5gQMi6mketK1Aad-_qiZoYvH7VU9sACLcB/s320/Screen%2BShot%2B2016-05-12%2Bat%2B11.49.02%2BAM.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"308\" height=\"320\"></a></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>However, when the checkbox is deselected, the plot looks like this, adding lines between the points. It should be noted that this is <b>not</b> a trend line. When there are more points, there are lines between all of them.:</div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-kCQH32QvupI/VzUiB_k8RrI/AAAAAAAAIn8/FSF4oAtcB1QSR1bJrtYUZ4_QqMsMfBg4QCLcB/s1600/Screen%2BShot%2B2016-05-12%2Bat%2B11.50.35%2BAM.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-kCQH32QvupI/VzUiB_k8RrI/AAAAAAAAIn8/FSF4oAtcB1QSR1bJrtYUZ4_QqMsMfBg4QCLcB/s1600/Screen%252BShot%252B2016-05-12%252Bat%252B11.50.35%252BAM.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393551178000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Jqfe9ME77dv0SF4rA7W6j\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-kCQH32QvupI/VzUiB_k8RrI/AAAAAAAAIn8/FSF4oAtcB1QSR1bJrtYUZ4_QqMsMfBg4QCLcB/s320/Screen%2BShot%2B2016-05-12%2Bat%2B11.50.35%2BAM.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"305\" height=\"320\"></a></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Is this a bug in shiny/ggplotly? Or is it an issue with my code? I&#39;ve provided a minimal example below</div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>    library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tidyr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dplyr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reshape</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">plotly</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>    df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;UserID&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0